WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:02.033
-Our first guest tonight

00:00:02.033 --> 00:00:03.434
is a Grammy Award-winning singer
and songwriter

00:00:03.434 --> 00:00:05.801
whose new album, "Chemistry,"
is available now.

00:00:05.801 --> 00:00:07.901
You also know her as the host
of "The Kelly Clarkson Show,"

00:00:07.901 --> 00:00:09.167
which airs weekdays.

00:00:09.167 --> 00:00:10.701
Check your local listings
for times.

00:00:10.701 --> 00:00:12.701
Please welcome back to the show
our friend and now neighbor

00:00:12.701 --> 00:00:14.334
Kelly Clarkson, everybody.

00:00:14.334 --> 00:00:16.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:23.734
♪♪

00:00:23.734 --> 00:00:31.067
♪♪

00:00:31.067 --> 00:00:32.634
Welcome back.

00:00:32.634 --> 00:00:34.400
-Oh, my God, I love your show.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.501
Do you know that you all
look like Smurfs

00:00:36.501 --> 00:00:37.667
on the TV back there?

00:00:37.667 --> 00:00:39.000
Like, everything is blue.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:42.000
-Everything is blue?
-You're all blue in the TV --

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.033
-In the dressing room --

00:00:43.033 --> 00:00:44.601
-No, right before
you enter the stage.

00:00:44.601 --> 00:00:46.367
-I see. Yeah.
-I was like, "Oh."

00:00:46.367 --> 00:00:47.868
-I've never seen myself on that,

00:00:47.868 --> 00:00:49.701
'cause when I'm back there,
I'm not on the screen.

00:00:49.701 --> 00:00:50.934
-Yeah, it would be tough.

00:00:50.934 --> 00:00:54.400
-I've tried
to run back and forth.

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:56.300
How are you?
-While inebriated.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:58.200
-You are new to the building.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:00:59.801
This is your first week
of shows here.

00:00:59.801 --> 00:01:02.200
Today was your first episode.
-You have been to my show.

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:04.200
-I was on your first episode.
What an honor.

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:05.534
-What an honor it was
to have you.

00:01:05.534 --> 00:01:07.734
You know I love you,
so it was an honor to have you.

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:09.434
-How do you like it so far,
being in 30 Rock?

00:01:09.434 --> 00:01:13.200
-I love it. I didn't really
realize the underground vibe.

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:14.701
Like, there's
so many restaurants.

00:01:14.701 --> 00:01:17.734
There's, like, a whole world.
like, underneath.

00:01:17.734 --> 00:01:20.400
Like, I didn't know.
-Wait until Christmas.

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:25.534
There's a giant tree outside
that's going to blow your mind.

00:01:25.534 --> 00:01:26.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:26.801 --> 00:01:28.334
-I knew that one.

00:01:28.334 --> 00:01:29.734
-And you've never
lived here before.

00:01:29.734 --> 00:01:31.100
This is your first time
living here.

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:32.634
-It's my first time living here.
And I love it.

00:01:32.634 --> 00:01:34.767
-I think this is
the perfect time of year

00:01:34.767 --> 00:01:36.200
to move to New York City.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:38.701
-I agree. Like, especially
for me personally, like,

00:01:38.701 --> 00:01:41.033
it helped that my kids
were like 100% into it.

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:42.300
-Oh, that's good.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:45.167
So it's helpful --
When they're happy, I'm happy.

00:01:45.167 --> 00:01:46.400
-Yeah. Right.
-Yeah.

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:48.534
-And how do they like it so far?
-They love it.

00:01:48.534 --> 00:01:50.801
-Are they excited
for their first Halloween

00:01:50.801 --> 00:01:52.267
in New York City?
-They are.

00:01:52.267 --> 00:01:53.868
But actually, the thing
they just got excited about --

00:01:53.868 --> 00:01:57.067
They've been to a show before
but not since we've lived here.

00:01:57.067 --> 00:01:58.334
And it was a long time ago.

00:01:58.334 --> 00:02:00.234
So they saw "Lion King"
the other night.

00:02:00.234 --> 00:02:04.167
And then I saw "Lion King"
three times yesterday

00:02:04.167 --> 00:02:07.234
'cause they re-enacted
the entire thing.

00:02:07.234 --> 00:02:08.300
And they're like,
"You know what?

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:09.434
I'm gonna do it over.
I can do better."

00:02:09.434 --> 00:02:10.834
And I'm like, "Oh,
we're gonna start fresh,

00:02:10.834 --> 00:02:13.234
aren't we, like, again.
Okay."

00:02:13.234 --> 00:02:15.100
-Like, "We're going to
go get our big puppets."

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:16.767
-Okay.

00:02:16.767 --> 00:02:20.601
-My wife took our 7-year-old
to "Lion King," and he loved it.

00:02:20.601 --> 00:02:25.133
But then they got
in a cab to go back downtown,

00:02:25.133 --> 00:02:27.067
and he has a very early bedtime.

00:02:27.067 --> 00:02:28.467
-Oh, so do my kids.
-Okay.

00:02:28.467 --> 00:02:30.601
-So his thing was --
-That's so we have a life.

00:02:30.601 --> 00:02:32.267
-Yeah. 100%.

00:02:32.267 --> 00:02:34.434
When people are like,
"My kids go to bed at 9:30,"

00:02:34.434 --> 00:02:36.767
I'm like, "And now why
don't you poison yourself?"

00:02:36.767 --> 00:02:39.100
-Yeah.
I'm like, "What?"

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:40.834
-"How do you
make your life happy?"

00:02:40.834 --> 00:02:43.601
-I will totally lie about
actually the time if I'm tired

00:02:43.601 --> 00:02:45.133
and be like, "Bedtime."

00:02:45.133 --> 00:02:47.000
Or my daughter's like,
"Are you sure?"

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:50.133
I'm like, "Totally sure.
Shut the blinds. It's fine."

00:02:50.133 --> 00:02:52.934
-This summer, I'd be like,
"It's nighttime,"

00:02:52.934 --> 00:02:54.501
and they'd pull the blinds back
and it would be like

00:02:54.501 --> 00:02:56.400
the sun would, like, blast in.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:57.701
-It's just weird.

00:02:57.701 --> 00:02:59.767
-So when she brought
my son home from "Lion King,"

00:02:59.767 --> 00:03:02.067
he'd never seen
Times Square at night.

00:03:02.067 --> 00:03:03.334
And so he saw "Lion King."

00:03:03.334 --> 00:03:04.667
But then he got home.
I'm like, "How was it?"

00:03:04.667 --> 00:03:08.601
He's like, "You can't believe
where we live."

00:03:08.601 --> 00:03:11.033
He's like, "You have
no idea what's happening

00:03:11.033 --> 00:03:13.267
just on a light level
in the city."

00:03:13.267 --> 00:03:15.267
-That was my kids, actually.

00:03:15.267 --> 00:03:17.000
That was probably the first time
that they've been

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:18.701
to Times Square,
like, at nighttime, yeah.

00:03:18.701 --> 00:03:20.501
-It's really awesome.
-It is. It's really magical.

00:03:20.501 --> 00:03:23.400
-When your kids realize
what New York City is...

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:25.334
-Yeah, and it keeps you busy.

00:03:25.334 --> 00:03:26.834
There's so many things
to do all the time.

00:03:26.834 --> 00:03:28.667
So, yeah.
-And now you obviously

00:03:28.667 --> 00:03:30.801
have hosted this show in L.A.,

00:03:30.801 --> 00:03:32.267
and I imagine
you're in a new studio.

00:03:32.267 --> 00:03:35.067
It's a little bit different,
but it must also feel like

00:03:35.067 --> 00:03:37.000
riding a bike
to some degree now.

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:39.300
-Yeah, I mean, honestly,
like, from the very first --

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:41.601
I like talking,
if you haven't noticed.

00:03:41.601 --> 00:03:43.734
So that part's very easy to me.

00:03:43.734 --> 00:03:45.567
I think the difference
for this season

00:03:45.567 --> 00:03:47.634
is I really needed
that fresh start,

00:03:47.634 --> 00:03:49.534
like, on a personal note,
just --

00:03:49.534 --> 00:03:52.467
Yeah, it's a rough few years,
and I just needed it.

00:03:52.467 --> 00:03:54.367
So I don't know
that I've done this show

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:55.968
like this kind of happy before.

00:03:55.968 --> 00:03:57.534
-That's wonderful to hear.

00:03:57.534 --> 00:03:58.601
-So, yeah.
-It comes across.

00:03:58.601 --> 00:04:00.133
-It does, yeah.

00:04:00.133 --> 00:04:02.601
-Also, I want to give
a shout-out.

00:04:02.601 --> 00:04:04.901
You had a very novel idea
for your first show.

00:04:04.901 --> 00:04:07.267
I was there, and the entire
audience was doormen.

00:04:07.267 --> 00:04:08.601
-Yes.
-New York City doormen

00:04:08.601 --> 00:04:09.934
and doorwomen.

00:04:09.934 --> 00:04:12.100
And what gave you that idea?

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:14.067
Why did you want to honor
our doormen and -women?

00:04:14.067 --> 00:04:17.300
-Well, we're meshing
our crew now, right?

00:04:17.300 --> 00:04:18.634
'Cause we have some from L.A.,
some from New York.

00:04:18.634 --> 00:04:20.200
And, like, I think a lot of us,
we just got here

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:21.567
and we're like,
"Wow, these are, like,

00:04:21.567 --> 00:04:24.033
essential people in your life
that you don't realize.

00:04:24.033 --> 00:04:26.334
You see every --
like, more than your family.

00:04:26.334 --> 00:04:28.267
And so -- And we were like,
"Yeah, let's do this."

00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:29.400
You know, a producer
came up with the idea,

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:31.400
and then it was just so magical.

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:33.267
You don't realize, like you
were talking about on my show,

00:04:33.267 --> 00:04:35.334
like, how your kids grow up
with these people.

00:04:35.334 --> 00:04:37.367
Like, you're always passing.
They're so helpful.

00:04:37.367 --> 00:04:39.734
It's like a part of your life
every day.

00:04:39.734 --> 00:04:41.334
-It's 100%.
-Yeah.

00:04:41.334 --> 00:04:46.133
-You had a leg up on decorating
your dressing rooms.

00:04:46.133 --> 00:04:48.200
-Well, I'm the Wayfair lady,
as well, so...

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:49.234
-Yes, you got that
going for you.

00:04:49.234 --> 00:04:50.667
-Yeah, I've got that
going for me.

00:04:50.667 --> 00:04:52.000
No, but I did actually.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:54.133
It's awesome, because anytime
we do decorate somewhere,

00:04:54.133 --> 00:04:55.334
I'm like, "Can I?"

00:04:55.334 --> 00:04:58.234
I always pull my discount
and I'm like, "Can I?"

00:04:58.234 --> 00:05:01.300
'Cause I have a new collection
'cause I love Montana so much.

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:04.934
And I actually really love the,
like, chic kind of ranch vibe.

00:05:04.934 --> 00:05:08.100
Like, that's my thing, so we
came up with a whole new thing.

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:09.467
So you might see that backstage
at my show.

00:05:09.467 --> 00:05:11.534
-You also talked briefly
at your show beforehand

00:05:11.534 --> 00:05:13.234
that you're into fantasy
football this year, first year.

00:05:13.234 --> 00:05:14.234
-Oh, my God.

00:05:14.234 --> 00:05:16.067
How did you do
this past weekend?

00:05:16.067 --> 00:05:17.801
-Monday night decides it.

00:05:17.801 --> 00:05:20.033
So when this airs,
I will know how it went,

00:05:20.033 --> 00:05:21.100
but it doesn't look good.

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:22.334
-It was not great for me.

00:05:22.334 --> 00:05:24.300
-But you also -- I said,
"Oh, that's so exciting.

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:26.167
You're doing it.
Who was your first pick?"

00:05:26.167 --> 00:05:28.901
And you said a name that
made me think you're bad at it.

00:05:28.901 --> 00:05:30.634
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.634 --> 00:05:33.167
-Here's the reason why.
Okay, now I'm into it.

00:05:33.167 --> 00:05:34.567
Now I know the players',
like, real names.

00:05:34.567 --> 00:05:36.000
-So on draft day,
you admit you blew it.

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:38.367
-But on draft day, I admit --
I didn't blow it,

00:05:38.367 --> 00:05:40.901
because I have Walker, Seattle,
and he's really good.

00:05:40.901 --> 00:05:42.367
Like, Walker III, what?
-But who'd you take first?

00:05:42.367 --> 00:05:44.033
Do you even remember who?
-I do.

00:05:44.033 --> 00:05:46.200
It was Kirk Cousins.
And here's the reason why.

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:49.267
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey.
He was ranked high.

00:05:49.267 --> 00:05:51.400
And then also, I met him
and I like him,

00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:54.667
and I like Cousins BBQ,
and so I was like, "Cool."

00:05:54.667 --> 00:05:57.801
-I mean, those are all
terrible reasons.

00:05:57.801 --> 00:05:59.234
-No, I'm not kidding.

00:05:59.234 --> 00:06:03.033
I picked Andrews from the Ravens
because I like Julie Andrews.

00:06:03.033 --> 00:06:07.834
I picked R. Wilson
'cause Rita Wilson is awesome.

00:06:07.834 --> 00:06:09.701
This is how I picked
my team at first.

00:06:09.701 --> 00:06:12.667
But now I studied up
and I realized on NFL+,

00:06:12.667 --> 00:06:14.200
you can go back and watch.

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:15.767
If you have the premium,
you can go back and watch games.

00:06:15.767 --> 00:06:18.067
Now I'm studying up.
Now I know players.

00:06:18.067 --> 00:06:20.300
I was talking to Erin backstage.
I'm ready for next season.

00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:21.601
-Well, I think maybe next year.

00:06:21.601 --> 00:06:23.267
I think next year
is where you start.

00:06:23.267 --> 00:06:26.367
-No, I did kill it, like,
a couple weeks so far.

00:06:26.367 --> 00:06:28.133
Just not this one.
-By the way, this really

00:06:28.133 --> 00:06:30.300
is bringing home the idea

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:32.033
that fantasy football
is different than football

00:06:32.033 --> 00:06:33.467
if you're basically
drafting people

00:06:33.467 --> 00:06:34.868
because they remind you
of Julie Andrews

00:06:34.868 --> 00:06:37.234
and you're doing
as well as I am.

00:06:37.234 --> 00:06:39.334
-When you don't know
the people, you don't know --

00:06:39.334 --> 00:06:40.334
I'm like, "I don't know.

00:06:40.334 --> 00:06:41.667
They have a lot of points,
it says."

00:06:41.667 --> 00:06:44.767
And the projections?
Whatever. They lie.

00:06:44.767 --> 00:06:46.300
-Yeah.
-Liars.

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:48.067
-You know what?
We finally agree on something.

00:06:48.067 --> 00:06:50.300
The projections?
-The projections are lying.

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:51.567
-Liars.

00:06:51.567 --> 00:06:53.267
You guys, this is very exciting.

00:06:53.267 --> 00:06:55.000
Kelly Clarkson!

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:57.968
Fifth season of
"The Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:06:57.968 --> 00:06:59.133
airs weekdays.

00:06:59.133 --> 00:07:00.334
Check your local listings.

00:07:00.334 --> 00:07:03.200
Her fantastic new album,
"Chemistry," is out now.

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:05.300
Stick around. We'll be right
back with Erin Andrews.

